{"title":"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. What is the width of the rectangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d859b636d878f6dd20381181ca4c6918fca9e0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{5}{9} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{14}{15} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"417\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the width of the rectangle. Using the length of the rectangle and the formula for the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a240500ceb451f21469afd5b504f36102a32ede2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}w = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6caaf35840c90bf40a934be9b257e0e6e49455d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\frac{1}{3} \\div \\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa30887ecaec84931f3a87ddad0e778442c54ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\frac{1 \\times 5}{3 \\times 3} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{5}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"167\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, because the area of a rectangle is its width multiplied by its length, we can realize that the width's denominator must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the length's denominator was not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the area has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in its denominator. This eliminates all of the answer choices except B and C.\n</p><p>We can also realize that the numerator must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to cancel out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the denominator of the length because the area's denominator wasn't divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This eliminates answer choice C.\n</p><p>All of the other answer choices have been eliminated, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12b3ee3f089bfdef8b8f1215e4025842c8f0db9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{5}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley\">2010 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\"